name        = "NS2 SUD Server Admin"
source_dir  = "source"
output_dir  = "output"
description = "[b]This mod is whitelisted.[/b]

[h1]NS2 SUD Server Admin[/h1]
Server tools for the NS2 Sudamerica server.

The scope of this mod is bound to simplify admin workload and ease the experience of the players of NS2 Sudamerica. This mod will never enact gameplay or balance changes of any kind.

Current features: consecutive rounds played and minutes played, to simplify spectator rotation so everyone gets to play; everyone joining as a spectator; the closest commander matchups before a round; a pause for Thunderdome and passworded games; disconnected players keeping their place in the round; the SUD Queue, which pairs up players waiting to get into a 6v6 or 7v7; all talk between rounds; and a skill requirement admins can switch on for a server.

[h1]Commands and language[/h1]
[list]
[*]Type [b]!help[/b] in chat for the full list of commands, printed in your console
[*]Type [b]!lang es[/b], [b]!lang pt[/b] or [b]!lang en[/b] to get the messages only you see in Spanish, Portuguese or English. The server remembers your choice
[/list]

[h1]Matches in a row[/h1]
[list]
[*]Type [b]!streakr[/b] in chat to see the top 5 players by rounds in a row, or [b]!streakm[/b] for the top 5 by minutes played over them. Only you see the answer
[*]Type [b]sud_streaks[/b] in the console for the full list of every player, ranked by rounds and by minutes
[*]When a spectator is waiting for a slot, anyone can check who has had their turn
[*]Sit a round out and your count goes back to 0
[*]Subbing in partway through a round counts as sitting it out, so helping a team never costs you
[*]Joining a team in the first 2 minutes of a round counts as playing it, even if you step out later
[*]Counts carry over map changes and start fresh each play session. Rounds shorter than 1 minute don't add to your round count, but the minutes you played still count
[/list]

[h1]Spectator on connect[/h1]
[list]
[*]Everyone who joins the server starts as a spectator, so nobody takes up a player slot just by waiting in the ready room. Thunderdome games are the exception
[*]Join a team from spectator whenever a player slot is free
[*]After a map change, players who were already on the server start in the ready room as usual
[/list]

[h1]Commander match[/h1]
[list]
[*]Before a round starts, when someone takes a command chair and the other team has no commander yet, chat shows the 5 players whose commander skill for the other team is closest
[*]Each name shows the gap: + means above the new commander, - means below
[*]Players who have never commanded are left out
[*]Type [b]!mycomm[/b] any time to see your own list. On a team you get the list for your team's chair, from spectator or the ready room you get both. Only you see it
[*]Type [b]!comm[/b] to see the list again for the commander in the chair, when only one chair is taken. Only you see it
[*]Not on Thunderdome games
[/list]

[h1]Pause[/h1]
[list]
[*]Only on Thunderdome and passworded games. When a round starts, chat says the pause is on
[*]Type [b]pause[/b] in chat during a round to pause the game after a 5 second countdown. Each team has 4 pauses per round
[*]To resume, someone on each team types [b]unpause[/b]. The game resumes on its own after 5 minutes
[*]If a player disconnects, the game pauses by itself
[/list]

[h1]Disconnected players[/h1]
[list]
[*]If you disconnect during a round, your player stays where it was, marked [D/C], with your lifeform, weapons, upgrades and resources
[*]Only if you were alive. If you were dead, or your player dies while you are away, you get your resources back when you rejoin your team
[*]Commanders are only kept in Thunderdome and passworded games. In a public game a commander who disconnects is removed, so someone else can take the chair or hive right away
[*]Reconnect before anyone takes your place and you go straight back in
[*]Anyone who joins your team takes your place, with everything you had
[*]Admins, and your team's commander, can swap you back in with [b]sud_swap[/b] in the console
[/list]

[h1]SUD Queue[/h1]
New in 1.3 and still being tested on live games.
[list]
[*]During a live 6v6 or 7v7 with the teams locked, type [b]!joinq[/b] from spectator or the ready room to wait for a place in the SUD Queue. The scoreboard shows you as SUD Queue
[*]As a spectator, pressing [b]F4[/b] does the same as [b]!joinq[/b]
[*]Spectators who are not in the SUD Queue get a reminder 30 seconds into the round and every minute after
[*]When you and another waiting player can join, one per team, and keep the difference in the teams' average elo within 75, chat announces you both and you get 30 seconds to type [b]!readyq[/b]. Your game window flashes on the taskbar
[*]The first pair of a round is picked 30 seconds in, from everyone who typed [b]!joinq[/b] by then, so it is not a race to be first
[*]Once both of you are ready, you join the teams that keep the game closest. Marine and alien skill differ for each player, so the server also picks who goes where
[*]Miss the 30 seconds and you leave the SUD Queue. The other player keeps their place
[*][b]!exitq[/b] leaves the SUD Queue, [b]!listq[/b] shows who is waiting
[*]Admins can switch it off for the rest of the round with [b]sud_joinpool off[/b] in the console
[*]Off on Thunderdome games
[/list]

[h1]All talk[/h1]
[list]
[*]When a round ends, and when a map loads, all talk is switched on so everyone can hear each other
[*]It stays on until an admin turns it off with [b]!alltalk[/b]
[*]Not on Thunderdome games
[/list]

[h1]Skill requirement[/h1]
New in 1.6.
[list]
[*]Admins can set a minimum Hive skill tier for a server, with exceptions they choose. Players below it can stay and spectate
[*]To check those exceptions, the server may look up a player's country from their IP address with ip-api.com. Only the country comes back, and it is not saved
[*]If your Hive skill hasn't loaded yet, you wait in spectator for a few seconds, since team shuffles and balance need it. If it doesn't load, reconnect
[*]Admins let a player in with [b]sud_allow[/b] in the console, or the Sud Allow button in Shine's admin menu
[*]Not on Thunderdome or passworded games
[/list]

The pause and the handling of disconnected players are ported from Dragon's NSL Mod.
"
image       = "preview.jpg"
